      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}P(A\\cap B)&=P(A)+P(B)-P(A\\cup B)\\\\P(A\\cap B)&=0.2+0.7-0.76\\\\P(A\\cap B)&=0.14\\\\P(A)P(B)&=0.2\\times0.7=0.14\\end{align*}$$\nSince $P(A\\cap B)=P(A)P(B)$, $A$ and $B$ are independent.",
